**PASS.** I watched the current build load cold at http://localhost:8000 and start correctly, and found no loading or startup defect to assign to a coder.

**Build tested:** commit e500c44 plus uncommitted changes. The diff hash starts 92e25d72 and `doom.wasm` starts 7afb94fa, both the same as all prior reports. `dist/` was already up to date, so I didn't rebuild. `artifacts/specification.md` and `artifacts/acceptance-criteria.md` don't exist.

**Server:** nothing was listening on port 8000, so I started my own server on `dist/`. All 7 files it served returned 200 and matched the hashes in `dist/`. I stopped only that server at the end, and port 8000 is free again.

**What I saw in the browser (Playwright, Chromium, with the cache cleared):**
- **Loading:** all 7 files loaded with status 200. There were no failed requests, page errors, console errors or console warnings.
- **First frame:** the title screen appeared fully drawn, in correct colours, by 282 ms after navigation. I checked the screenshot by eye: no red/blue swap.
- **Speed:** the game ran at 35.11 tics per second, within the 31.5–38.5 range. The longest gap between frames was 10.4 ms, so the page never froze.
- **Esc menu:** it opened over the demo and closed again, and the demo kept running behind it. The yellow tint in `menu-closed.png` is Doom's normal flash after picking up armor, not a colour bug.
- **Shape:** the game keeps its 16:10 shape at both 1280x720 and 800x600, with no scrollbars.
- **One difference from last time:** the previous review saw 2 audio-autoplay warnings in the console. They didn't appear this time. I didn't look into why; they weren't counted as failures either way.

**Still open (carried over):**
- **Cosmetic, coder:** the browser tab shows "Doom (WASM)" for about 280 ms before the game renames it to "DOOM Shareware".
- **Tester:** speed and freeze checks must allow for the screen-wipe pause about 5 s after load, which lasts about 1 s. I measured after it this time, so I didn't re-check it.
- **Not checked:** Firefox and Safari, high-DPI screens, a real hidden tab, and whether the audio sounds right. These need a tester or a person.

The pass criteria are ones the agents proposed; you haven't approved them. There were no manual interventions. I edited no source, test or loop files and created no `result.json`.

